{
  "_note": "The handful of buckets a board actually talks about. Real establishments carry sixty department names — 'AP/AR', 'FP&A', 'Group Treasury', 'Payroll Services' — and comparing sixty units against each other answers nothing, because most are too small to compare and the ones that aren't are answering a question nobody asked. Rolling them into these buckets is what turns 'which function is bloated' into a sentence with Finance or Operations in it. The raw department is never overwritten; it is kept beside the bucket and every play still works on the real team, because merging a payroll team into treasury on the grounds that both are 'Finance' would be a redesign nobody asked for.",
  "_titles": "The same keywords place job titles, but only for positions whose department is missing or unplaceable — which is why role words ('nurse', 'carer', 'accountant') sit alongside team words here. A payroll export often carries a title and no department at all, and without this the whole establishment is one function called Unclassified with nothing to compare. Where a file states a department, the department wins and the title is never consulted.",
  "_matching": "A department is placed by the longest keyword it contains, so 'Financial Systems Engineering' lands on the more specific match rather than the first one tried. Keywords of three characters or fewer must appear as whole words — otherwise 'hr' places 'Thrive Programme' in People. Anything no keyword claims keeps its own name and is reported as unplaced, rather than being swept into a bucket it may not belong in.",
